{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short --branch; rg --files --hidden -g AGENTS.md -g '\"'!.git/**'\"' .; sed -n '1,280p' host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; cat host/gambit/profiles.ss; cat host/gambit/unbound-allowlist.txt\"","aggregated_output":"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-6ZcOjVOJ' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-19 11:46:14.390 xcodebuild[21502:142799268]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-19 11:46:14.724 xcodebuild[21502:142799266] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-fArMiK9G' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-19 11:46:15.640 xcodebuild[21524:142799335]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-19 11:46:15.920 xcodebuild[21524:142799334] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n## gambit-ffi-p1b\n;; host-ffi.ss — the jolt.ffi host-owned surface for the GAMBIT target\n;; (P1b-stage1). On Chez these vars live in host/chez/java/ffi.ss, which the\n;; gambit boot manifest excludes — without this file every jolt.ffi name was an\n;; unbound global (the same shape the host-vars.ss degradation fixed for\n;; clojure.core). Stage-1 binds the memory/loader/errno surface the qualified\n;; tier backs (the adapter rows + the native bridge), implements what the\n;; stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj public functions call into, and binds EVERYTHING ELSE to\n;; a message-carrying refusal — nothing stays unbound, nothing pretends.\n;;\n;; Loaded after host-vars.ss, before the seed image (same rule: these bindings\n;; are the last word for the names the excluded ffi.ss owned). Requires the\n;; booted kernel (jolt-nil, def-var!, jolt-hash-map, make-pvec, ...) — this\n;; file is boot-world only; the sa-* tier it leans on also loads standalone\n;; under gambitcheck without it.\n\n(define (joltffi-public-error thunk)\n  (guard (e (#t (throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException\n                            (or (condition-message e) \"jolt.ffi: native bridge failure\"))))\n    (thunk)))\n\n(define (joltffi-public-blocking-raise)\n  (joltffi-public-error sa-foreign-procedure-blocking-raise))\n\n(define (joltffi-public-procedure args ret name variadic capture?)\n  (let ((fp (joltffi-public-error\n             (lambda () ((if capture? joltffi-foreign-capture-procedure joltffi-foreign-procedure)\n                         args ret name variadic)))))\n    (lambda args\n      (joltffi-public-error (lambda () (apply fp args))))))\n\n;; ---- emitted-text helpers the compiler's ordinary-call wrappers lean on -----\n;; The :string conversions invert per direction like the Chez pair; jolt truthy\n;; rule for :bool; jfloat unboxing for :float/:double. jolt-ffi-c->string maps\n;; the adapter's NULL-string #f to jolt-nil (values.ss's sentinel — bound by\n;; the time any of these RUN; the define only closes over it).\n(define (jolt-ffi-string->c x)\n  (cond ((string? x) x)\n        ((jolt-nil? x) #f)                ; nil IS NULL, in both directions\n        (else (throw-jvm 'IllegalArgumentException\n                         (string-append \"jolt.ffi: :string got \" (jolt-pr-str x)\n                                        \" — NULL is spelled nil\")))))\n(define (jolt-ffi-c->string x) (if x x jolt-nil))\n(define (jolt-ffi-bool->c v) (if (or (jolt-nil? v) (eq? v #f)) 0 1))\n(define (jolt-ffi-c->bool raw) (not (eqv? (jnum->exact raw) 0)))\n(define (jolt-ffi-float->c x) (if (jfloat? x) (jfloat-fl x) x))\n\n;; A :string ARGUMENT travels as u8* on Chez (an immobile copy). Gambit has no\n;; immobile allocation and the stage-1 bridge carries no :string-argument shape\n;; (the registry has none), so this raises BEFORE the unbound-identifier fate\n;; the pre-stage1 boot would have dealt: the adapter's shape validation refuses\n;; :string arguments, and this helper — which the emitted wrapper evaluates\n;; first — refuses for any path that might reach it out of order.\n(define (jolt-ffi-string-arg x)\n  (throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException\n             \"jolt.ffi: :string arguments are unsupported on the gambit target — no immobile allocation behind the stage-1 bridge\"))\n\n;; The emitted call keeps string copies live until C returns; identity here,\n;; because nothing that evaluates it can have a live foreign reference (the\n;; string-arg path above refuses first). Bound so the emitted TEXT never dies\n;; on an unbound identifier at load.\n(define (keep-live x) x)\n\n;; jolt-ffi-function-pointer: the pointer-call null guard (backend\n;; ffi-pointer-procedure-expr emits it ahead of each call). Pointer-call\n;; bindings are compile-time-refused on :gambit, so this only guards paths that\n;; hand a raw address to the ordinary tier.\n(define (jolt-ffi-function-pointer ptr)\n  (let ((address (if (jolt-nil? ptr) 0 (jnum->exact ptr))))\n    (if (eqv? address 0)\n        (throw-jvm 'NullPointerException \"jolt.ffi: null C function pointer\")\n        address)))\n\n;; jolt-ffi-dlsym-native (the compiler's emitted scoped probe) is defined in\n;; the adapter itself — it must exist in every world the emitted text loads in,\n;; including the adapter-only gambitcheck unit.\n\n;; ---- foreign memory over the adapter tier -------------------------------------\n;; alloc returns the ADDRESS (an exact integer); read/write take the type\n;; keyword and the offset LAST (the babashka.ffi order the stdlib wrapper\n;; keeps). Type keywords arrive as jolt keywords; the stdlib resolves layouts\n;; and places before calling, so these see scalars only.\n(define (joltffi-keyword-name kw)\n  (if (keyword-t? kw) (keyword-t-name kw) kw))\n\n(define (joltffi-type->chez kw)\n  (let ((n (joltffi-keyword-name kw)))\n    (cond\n      ((string=? n \"int\") 'int)\n      ((string=? n \"uint\") 'unsigned-int)\n      ((or (string=? n \"int8\") (string=? n \"i8\")) 'integer-8)\n      ((or (string=? n \"uint8\") (string=? n \"u8\") (string=? n \"byte\")) 'unsigned-8)\n      ((or (string=? n \"int16\") (string=? n \"short\")) 'integer-16)\n      ((or (string=? n \"uint16\") (string=? n \"ushort\")) 'unsigned-16)\n      ((string=? n \"int32\") 'integer-32)\n      ((string=? n \"uint32\") 'unsigned-32)\n      ((string=? n \"long\") 'long)\n      ((string=? n \"ulong\") 'unsigned-long)\n      ((string=? n \"int64\") 'integer-64)\n      ((string=? n \"uint64\") 'unsigned-64)\n      ((string=? n \"size_t\") 'size_t)\n      ((string=? n \"ssize_t\") 'ssize_t)\n      ((string=? n \"iptr\") 'iptr)\n      ((string=? n \"uptr\") 'uptr)\n      ((string=? n \"double\") 'double)\n      ((string=? n \"float\") 'float)\n      ((or (string=? n \"pointer\") (string=? n \"void*\")) 'void*)\n      ((string=? n \"char\") 'char)\n      ((string=? n \"bool\") 'jolt-bool)   ; one byte wide; converted at the boundary\n      ((string=? n \"string\") 'string)\n      ((string=? n \"void\") 'void)\n      (else (error #f (string-append \"jolt.ffi: unknown foreign type :\" n))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-sizeof-chez ct) (sa-foreign-sizeof (if (eq? ct 'jolt-bool) 'unsigned-8 ct)))\n\n(define (joltffi-read ptr ty off)\n  (let ((ct (joltffi-type->chez ty)))\n    (cond\n      ((eq? ct 'jolt-bool)\n       (jolt-ffi-c->bool (sa-foreign-ref 'unsigned-8 (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off))))\n      ((eq? ct 'float)\n       (make-jfloat (sa-foreign-ref 'float (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off))))\n      ((eq? ct 'string)\n       (jolt-ffi-c->string (joltffi-read-string (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off))))\n      (else (sa-foreign-ref ct (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off))))))\n\n;; a NUL-terminated C string at ptr -> string (adapter-level #f for a NULL\n;; first byte means the caller spelled NULL with 0 — see ptr->string). One bulk\n;; move of the whole window, then a Scheme-side scan; the stdlib's ptr->string\n;; and the :string __read ride on this.\n(define (joltffi-read-string ptr off)\n  (let ((p (+ (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off))))\n    (if (= p 0) #f\n        (let scan ((n 0) (bytes '()))\n          (let ((v (sa-foreign-ref 'unsigned-8 p n)))\n            (if (= v 0)\n                (utf8->string (list->u8vector (reverse bytes)))\n                (scan (+ n 1) (cons v bytes))))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-write ptr ty val off)\n  (let ((ct (joltffi-type->chez ty)))\n    (cond\n      ((eq? ct 'jolt-bool)\n       (sa-foreign-set! 'unsigned-8 (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off) (jolt-ffi-bool->c val)))\n      ((memq ct '(float double))\n       (sa-foreign-set! ct (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off) (jolt-ffi-float->c val)))\n      ((eq? ct 'string)\n       (let ((s (jolt-ffi-string->c val)))\n         (if s\n             (let ((bv (string->utf8 s)))\n               (sa-foreign-bytes-set! (+ (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off)) bv (bytevector-length bv))\n               (let ((z (make-bytevector 1 0)))\n                 (sa-foreign-bytes-set! (+ (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off) (bytevector-length bv)) z 1))\n               jolt-nil)\n             jolt-nil)))\n      (else (sa-foreign-set! ct (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off) val)))\n    jolt-nil))\n\n;; ---- the size bookkeeping ------------------------------------------------------\n;; jolt.ffi/size answers what jolt was TOLD — arena allocations, segments. One\n;; table, address -> size, guarded by the adapter's loader mutex's sibling.\n(define joltffi-sizes-mu (make-mutex))\n(define joltffi-sizes (make-eqv-hashtable))\n(define (joltffi-remember-size! ptr n)\n  (jwm-call joltffi-sizes-mu (lambda () (hashtable-set! joltffi-sizes (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact n))))\n  jolt-nil)\n(define (joltffi-forget-sizes! ps)\n  (jwm-call joltffi-sizes-mu\n    (lambda ()\n      (for-each (lambda (p) (hashtable-delete! joltffi-sizes (jnum->exact p)))\n                (seq->list (jolt-seq ps)))))\n  jolt-nil)\n(define (joltffi-recorded-size ptr)\n  (jwm-call joltffi-sizes-mu (lambda () (hashtable-ref joltffi-sizes (jnum->exact ptr) 0))))\n\n;; ---- alloc/free ------------------------------------------------------------------\n(define (joltffi-alloc nbytes)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact nbytes))\n         (p (sa-foreign-alloc n)))\n    (when (> n 0) (joltffi-remember-size! p n))\n    p))\n(define (joltffi-calloc nbytes)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact nbytes))\n         (p (sa-foreign-alloc n)))\n    (when (> n 0)\n      (sa-foreign-zero! p n)\n      (joltffi-remember-size! p n))\n    p))\n(define (joltffi-host-free ptr)\n  (sa-foreign-free (jnum->exact ptr))\n  (jwm-call joltffi-sizes-mu\n    (lambda () (hashtable-delete! joltffi-sizes (jnum->exact ptr))))\n  jolt-nil)\n(define (joltffi-copy src dst n)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact n)) (bv (make-bytevector n)))\n    (when (> n 0)\n      (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! (jnum->exact src) bv n)\n      (sa-foreign-bytes-set! (jnum->exact dst) bv n))\n    jolt-nil))\n(define (joltffi-null? ptr) (and (number? ptr) (= (jnum->exact ptr) 0)))\n(define joltffi-null 0)\n\n;; read/write take (ptr ty [off]) — the babashka.ffi offset-last order\n(define joltffi-read-fn\n  (case-lambda ((ptr ty) (joltffi-read ptr ty 0))\n               ((ptr ty off) (joltffi-read ptr ty off))))\n(define joltffi-write-fn\n  (case-lambda ((ptr ty val) (joltffi-write ptr ty val 0))\n               ((ptr ty val off) (joltffi-write ptr ty val off))))\n\n;; ---- buffer I/O (known length) ---------------------------------------------------\n(define (joltffi-read-bytes ptr n)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact n)) (p (jnum->exact ptr)) (bv (make-bytevector n)))\n    (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! p bv n)\n    (guard (e (#t (list->string (map integer->char (bytevector->u8-list bv)))))\n      (utf8->string bv))))\n(define (joltffi-write-bytes ptr s)\n  (let* ((bv (string->utf8 s)) (n (bytevector-length bv)) (p (jnum->exact ptr)))\n    (sa-foreign-bytes-set! p bv n)\n    n))\n\n;; ptr->string: NUL-terminated C string at ptr (NULL/0 -> nil)\n(define joltffi-ptr->string\n  (case-lambda\n    ((p) (joltffi-ptr->string* p #f))\n    ((p limit) (joltffi-ptr->string* p (if (jolt-nil? limit) #f (jnum->exact limit))))))\n(define (joltffi-ptr->string* ptr limit)\n  (if (joltffi-null? ptr) jolt-nil\n      (let ((p (jnum->exact ptr)))\n        (let scan ((n 0) (bytes '()))\n          (when (and limit (>= n limit))\n            (throw-jvm 'IllegalArgumentException \"jolt.ffi/ptr->string: no NUL byte within the limit\"))\n          (let ((v (sa-foreign-ref 'unsigned-8 p n)))\n            (if (= v 0) (utf8->string (list->u8vector (reverse bytes)))\n                (scan (+ n 1) (cons v bytes))))))))\n(define (joltffi-string->ptr s)\n  (if (jolt-nil? s) 0\n      (let* ((bv (string->utf8 (jolt-str-render-one s)))\n             (n (bytevector-length bv))\n             (p (sa-foreign-alloc (+ n 1))))\n        (guard (e (#t (sa-foreign-free p) (raise e)))\n          (sa-foreign-bytes-set! p bv n)\n          (sa-foreign-set! 'unsigned-8 p n 0)\n          (joltffi-remember-size! p (+ n 1))\n          p))))\n(define (joltffi-utf8-length s)\n  (if (jolt-nil? s) 0 (bytevector-length (string->utf8 (jolt-str-render-one s)))))\n\n;; ---- loader surface ---------------------------------------------------------------\n;; load-library: the Chez semantics minus Windows/Termux arms — nil keeps the\n;; boot's process handle; a per-OS map selects this platform's entry; anything\n;; else is one name or an ORDERED candidate list, tried in order, with the\n;; loader's own reason preserved on failure. Answers {:path \"<loaded>\"} or nil.\n(define (joltffi-library-map path)\n  (jolt-hash-map (keyword #f \"path\") path))\n\n(define (joltffi-candidate-list name)\n  (if (or (pvec? name) (jolt-seq? name) (jolt-lazyseq? name))\n      (map (lambda (c) (if (string? c) c (jolt-str-render-one c))) (seq->list (jolt-seq name)))\n      (list (jolt-str-render-one name))))\n\n(define (joltffi-load-failure-note cands)\n  (let loop ((cs cands) (acc '()))\n    (if (null? cs)\n        (and (pair? acc)\n             (let join ((xs (reverse acc)) (out \"\"))\n               (if (null? xs)\n                   out\n                   (join (cdr xs) (if (string=? out \"\") (car xs)\n                                      (string-append out \"; \" (car xs)))))))\n        (let* ((cand (car cs))\n               (exists (guard (e (#t #f)) (file-exists? cand)))\n               (why (jwm-call joltffi-native-mu\n                      (lambda () (hashtable-ref joltffi-native-failures cand #f)))))\n          (loop (cdr cs)\n                (if exists\n                    (cons (string-append cand \" is there but did not load\"\n                                         (if why (string-append \": \" why) \"\"))\n                          acc)\n                    acc))))))\n\n;; profiles.ss — how much of the language a Gambit build carries.\n;;\n;; DATA, read by gen-boot.ss (on Chez) to write a boot file per profile. Not\n;; loaded at runtime.\n;;\n;; boot.ss stays the single source of load ORDER. This file only says which of\n;; its files belong to an OPTIONAL feature group, and which profile keeps which\n;; groups. Anything boot.ss includes that is not named in a group here is the\n;; kernel: always in, not selectable.\n;;\n;; Excluding a group does two things. Its files are left out of the generated\n;; boot, and every clojure.core name those files define is bound to a raise that\n;; says the group was excluded — DERIVED by scanning the files for def-var!\n;; forms, so the error surface tracks the code instead of a hand-kept list. A\n;; dropped feature reports itself; it never fails as an unbound global.\n;;\n;; Measured cost of each group in the js bundle (raw / gzipped, which is what a\n;; web server ships):\n;;\n;;   regex      2.4 MB / 0.4 MB\n;;   compiler   2.9 MB / 0.5 MB\n;;   core       8.7 MB / 0.7 MB\n;;   ---------------------------\n;;   kernel    19.4 MB / 2.1 MB   floor: the Gambit runtime plus jolt's kernel\n;;   full      31.0 MB / 3.3 MB\n;;\n;; The floor dominates, so profiles trade features for the last third of the\n;; bundle. Adding a group is worth it when it is separable AND measurable; a\n;; group worth kilobytes is churn.\n\n(groups\n\n  ;; Runtime regex: irregex plus the Java-pattern translation in front of it.\n  ;; Without it re-pattern/re-find/re-seq/re-matches and #\"...\" literals raise.\n  (regex\n   \"regex\"\n   (\"../../vendor/irregex/irregex.scm\"\n    \"../chez/java/regex-translate.ss\"\n    \"../chez/regex.ss\"))\n\n  ;; clojure.core itself, as emitted by the cross-mint, plus the native\n  ;; re-assertions over it. Excluding this leaves the kernel and no standard\n  ;; library — an embedding, not a Clojure.\n  (core\n   \"clojure.core\"\n   (\"seed/prelude.ss\"\n    \"../chez/post-prelude.ss\"\n    \"host-vars.ss\"))\n\n  ;; The compiler image and the read-analyze-emit-eval path over it. Excluding\n  ;; it gives a runtime that can hold and print jolt values but cannot compile\n  ;; source, so there is no eval, no REPL, and no runtime macro expansion.\n  (compiler\n   \"compiler\"\n   (\"seed/image.ss\"\n    \"../chez/compile-eval.ss\")))\n\n(profiles\n\n  ;; Everything. What `make gambitcheck`, `gambitkernel` and `gambiteval` run\n  ;; against, and the default for a bundle.\n  (full    (regex core compiler))\n\n  ;; The browser REPL: it must compile what a visitor types, and clojure.core is\n  ;; the language, so both stay. Regex is the one feature a REPL demo can lose\n  ;; and still be a REPL.\n  (repl    (core compiler))\n\n  ;; The floor, for measuring and for embedding: kernel only, no standard\n  ;; library and no compiler.\n  (kernel  ()))\n# unbound-allowlist.txt — Scheme globals the Gambit boot references and DOES NOT\n# define, each on a path this target never takes.\n#\n# One name per line, grouped under a comment that says why the group is\n# unreachable here. host/gambit/unbound-check.ss (make gambitunbound) pins\n# this against Gambit's own linker report over the full-profile boot: a name\n# missing from this list fails the gate, and so does a line whose name has\n# since been defined — the list only shrinks truthfully. `make\n# gambitunbound-regen` keeps the comments and still-valid lines in place,\n# drops stale lines and appends new names at the end for classification.\n#\n# A name here is a documented gap, not a free pass: reaching it raises\n# \"Unbound variable\" with no jolt context. Binding it — a mirror in\n# rt-core.ss, a shim in prelude-shims.ss, a raise naming the absent\n# capability — is always better than a line here.\n#\n# gsi runtime names the js link file does not carry. Every site is guarded\n# and answers a fallback when the name is missing: sa-bytes-allocated (0),\n# scheme-version (\"Gambit Scheme\"), the equal?-hash probe (a string fold),\n# %jolt-interaction-environment (interaction-environment first).\n##bytes-allocated\n##version-string\nequal?-hash\nrepl-environment\n#\n# compile-eval.ss's source-annotated eval (jolt-eval-with-source): Chez's\n# annotation APIs behind (jolt-ce-trace-frames?), which no hook sets here —\n# tracing is the excluded source-registry.ss's, and the plain eval path runs.\nget-datum/annotations\nmake-source-file-descriptor\nnative-transcoder\nopen-bytevector-input-port\ntranscoded-port\njolt-register-eval-marker-table!\n#\n# compile-eval.ss's data-reader pass: the loader's flag is read under a guard\n# (#f when unbound) and the apply step runs only when it was set.\ndata-readers-active\nldr-apply-readers\n#\n# The accessors behind the value predicates rt-core.ss answers #f for: an\n# inst, a BigDecimal, an array and a host reader cannot be built here, so the\n# arms that read them (format's %f, the array class tags, the char[] arms of\n# StringBuilder's append/insert/getChars behind char-array-arg?, the reader\n# protocols in post-prelude.ss and clojure.edn/read) are never entered.\ninst-rfc3339\nchar-array->string\nchar-array-chunk\nja-len\nja-set!\njolt-array-vec\njbigdec->string\njbigdec-scale\njbigdec-unscaled\njolt-bigdec-from-string\njolt-inst-from-string\nchez-edn-read\nchez-line-seq\nhost-reader-read\n#\n# Emitted for clojure.core.Vec's node writes (vector-of, 60-gvec.clj); no\n# array constructor exists here, so no Vec is ever built.\njolt-aset3\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '300,380p' host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; cat host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-public.ss; sed -n '450,468p' host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss; sed -n '2120,2140p' Makefile; cat host/gambit/unbound-check.sh; sed -n '1,150p' host/gambit/unbound-check.ss; sed -n '1,95p' host/chez/java/ffi.ss; rg -n 'ffi-str-arg|ffi-type->chez|ffi-loaded\\\\?|ffi-find-symbol|ffi-defining-libraries' host/chez/java/ffi.ss; tail -20 /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795062317148-reviewer-p1b-stage1-argon.gemini-4-argon.findings.md; sed -n '1,155p' host/gambit/gen-boot.ss\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '300,380p' host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; cat host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-public.ss; sed -n '450,468p' host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss; sed -n '2120,2140p' Makefile; cat host/gambit/unbound-check.sh; sed -n '1,150p' host/gambit/unbound-check.ss; sed -n '1,95p' host/chez/java/ffi.ss; rg -n 'ffi-str-arg|ffi-type->chez|ffi-loaded\\\\?|ffi-find-symbol|ffi-defining-libraries' host/chez/java/ffi.ss; tail -20 /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795062317148-reviewer-p1b-stage1-argon.gemini-4-argon.findings.md; sed -n '1,155p' host/gambit/gen-boot.ss\"","aggregated_output":"      ((joltffi-load-native (car cs)) (car cs))\n      (else (loop (cdr cs))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-load-library . args)\n  (cond\n    ((or (null? args) (jolt-nil? (car args)))\n     jolt-nil)\n    ((jolt-map? (car args))\n     (let* ((spec (car args))\n            (key (begin (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'jolt.ffi/load-library) (joltffi-platform-key)))\n            (name (jolt-get-dispatch spec (keyword #f key) jolt-nil))\n            (name (if (and (jolt-nil? name) (string=? key \"darwin\"))\n                      (jolt-get-dispatch spec (keyword #f \"mac\") jolt-nil) name)))\n       (when (jolt-nil? name)\n         (jolt-throw (jolt-ex-info\n                       (string-append \"jolt.ffi/load-library: no :\" key \" entry in the per-OS spec\") spec)))\n       (joltffi-library-map (joltffi-load-candidates (joltffi-candidate-list name)))))\n    (else (joltffi-library-map (joltffi-load-candidates (joltffi-candidate-list (car args)))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-loaded? name)\n  (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'jolt.ffi/loaded?)\n  (if (joltffi-load-native name) #t #f))\n\n(define (joltffi-system-library-candidates n)\n  (list (string-append \"lib\" n \".dylib\") (string-append n \".dylib\")))\n\n(define (joltffi-load-system-library name)\n  (joltffi-library-map\n   (joltffi-load-candidates\n    (joltffi-system-library-candidates (if (string? name) name (jolt-str-render-one name))))))\n\n(define joltffi-find-symbol\n  (case-lambda\n    ((sym)\n     (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'jolt.ffi/find-symbol)\n     (let* ((n (if (string? sym) sym (jolt-str-render-one sym)))\n            (a (joltffi-dlsym-loaded n)))\n       (cond (a a)\n             ((guard (e (#t #f)) (sa-foreign-entry? n)) (sa-foreign-entry-address n))\n             (else jolt-nil))))\n    ((lib sym)\n     (if (jolt-nil? lib)\n         (joltffi-find-symbol sym)\n         (let* ((n (if (string? sym) sym (jolt-str-render-one sym)))\n                (path (and (jolt-map? lib)\n                           (jolt-get-dispatch lib (keyword #f \"path\") jolt-nil)))\n                (h (and (string? path) (joltffi-library-handle path))))\n           (unless h\n             (jolt-throw (jolt-ex-info\n                           \"jolt.ffi/find-symbol: no handle for this library — pass the map load-library answered for it\"\n                           (jolt-hash-map (keyword #f \"library\") lib))))\n           (let ((a (joltffi-dlsym h n)))\n             (if (and a (not (= a 0))) a jolt-nil)))))))\n\n;; the dlopen handle a load-library of PATH registered, or #f\n(define (joltffi-library-handle path)\n  (let loop ((hs joltffi-native-handles))\n    (cond ((null? hs) #f)\n          ((string=? (caar hs) path) (cdar hs))\n          (else (loop (cdr hs))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-defining-libraries sym)\n  (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'jolt.ffi/defining-libraries)\n  (make-pvec\n   (list->vector\n    (map car (joltffi-definers (if (string? sym) sym (jolt-str-render-one sym)))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-load-failure-note-var cands)\n  (joltffi-load-failure-note (if (list? cands) cands (list cands))))\n\n;; ---- refusing rows (message-carrying; the capability stays unqualified) -------\n(define (joltffi-refuse-fn name reason)\n  (lambda args\n    (jolt-throw\n     (jolt-host-throwable\n      \"java.lang.UnsupportedOperationException\"\n      (string-append \"jolt.ffi/\" name \" is unsupported on the gambit target: \" reason)))))\n\n(define (joltffi-refuse-var! name reason)\n  (def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" name (joltffi-refuse-fn name reason)))\n\n;; Target-identified, booted compiler/eval public path, without Chez execution.\n(##include \"../boot.ss\")\n(define failures 0)\n(define checks 0)\n(define (public-check src expected)\n  (set! checks (+ checks 1))\n  (let ((got (guard (e (#t (string-append \"HOST-ERROR: \" (or (condition-message e) (object->string e)))))\n               (jolt-pr-readable (jolt-compile-eval src \"user\")))))\n    (if (equal? got expected)\n        (printf \"  ok     ~a => ~a\\n\" src got)\n        (begin (set! failures (+ failures 1))\n               (printf \"  FAIL   ~a => ~s expected ~s\\n\" src got expected)))))\n(public-check \"(jolt.backend-scheme.session/target)\" \":gambit\")\n(public-check \"(:path (jolt.ffi/load-library \\\"build/gambit-ffi/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib\\\"))\" \"\\\"build/gambit-ffi/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib\\\"\")\n(public-check \"((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_layout_version\\\" [] :int))\" \"42\")\n(public-check \"((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_eintr\\\" [] :int32))\" \"4\")\n(public-check \"(let [p (jolt.ffi/alloc 16)] (try (jolt.ffi/write p :uint64 18446744073709551615 1) (jolt.ffi/read p :uint64 1) (finally (jolt.ffi/free p))))\" \"18446744073709551615N\")\n(public-check \"(let [p (jolt.ffi/string->ptr \\\"é\\\")] (try (jolt.ffi/ptr->string p) (finally (jolt.ffi/free p))))\" \"\\\"é\\\"\")\n(public-check \"((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_errtext\\\" [:int] :string) 1)\" \"\\\"joltffi-error-one\\\"\")\n(public-check \"((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_errtext\\\" [:int] :string) 0)\" \"nil\")\n(public-check \"((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_vfcntl\\\" [:int :int :varargs :int] :int) 10 3 100)\" \"113\")\n(public-check \"(let [f (jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_socketlike\\\" [:int :int :int] :int {:capture-native-error true}) e (jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_eacces\\\" [] :int)] (= (f -1 0 0) [-1 (e)]))\" \"true\")\n(public-check \"((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_scalar_10\\\" [:float] :float) (float 0.25))\" \"0.25\")\n(public-check \"((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_scalar_1\\\" [:bool] :bool) false)\" \"false\")\n;; Refusal guards must execute under the real :gambit emitter and stay catchable.\n(public-check \"(try (jolt.ffi/__layout [:struct [[:x :int]]]) (catch UnsupportedOperationException e :layout-refused))\" \":layout-refused\")\n(public-check \"(try ((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_layout_version\\\" [] :int :blocking)) (catch Throwable e (boolean (re-find #\\\"blocking ffi is unsupported\\\" (ex-message e)))))\" \"true\")\n(public-check \"(try ((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_socketlike\\\" [:int :int :int] :int {:blocking true :capture-native-error true}) -1 0 0) (catch Throwable e (boolean (re-find #\\\"blocking ffi is unsupported\\\" (ex-message e)))))\" \"true\")\n(public-check \"(try (jolt.ffi/__ccallable (fn [] 1) [] :int) (catch UnsupportedOperationException e :callable-refused))\" \":callable-refused\")\n(public-check \"(try (jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"f\\\" [[:by-value [:struct [[:x :int]]]]] :int) (catch UnsupportedOperationException e :aggregate-refused))\" \":aggregate-refused\")\n(public-check \"(try (jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"f\\\" [:int :&] :int) (catch UnsupportedOperationException e :runtime-tail-refused))\" \":runtime-tail-refused\")\n(public-check \"(try ((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_layout_version\\\" [:pointer :int] :pointer) 0 0) (catch Throwable e (boolean (re-find #\\\"unregistered shape\\\" (ex-message e)))))\" \"true\")\n(public-check \"(let [p (jolt.ffi/alloc 8)] (try (jolt.ffi/write-bytes p \\\"abc\\\") (jolt.ffi/read-bytes p 3) (finally (jolt.ffi/free p))))\" \"\\\"abc\\\"\")\n(public-check \"(:path (jolt.ffi/load-library {:darwin \\\"build/gambit-ffi/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib\\\"}))\" \"\\\"build/gambit-ffi/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib\\\"\")\n(public-check \"(try (jolt.ffi/load-library \\\"/nonexistent/libjoltffi-missing.dylib\\\") (catch Throwable e (boolean (re-find #\\\"cannot load\\\" (ex-message e)))))\" \"true\")\n(public-check \"(try (jolt.ffi/load-library \\\"build/gambit-ffi/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib\\\") (catch Throwable e (boolean (re-find #\\\"is there but did not load.*libjoltffi-dep\\\" (ex-message e)))))\" \"true\")\n(public-check \"(boolean (jolt.ffi/find-symbol \\\"joltffi_fx_layout_version\\\"))\" \"true\")\n(public-check \"(jolt.ffi/find-symbol \\\"joltffi_absent\\\")\" \"nil\")\n(public-check \"((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_vsetopt\\\" [:pointer :int :varargs :pointer] :int) 0 7 0)\" \"7\")\n(public-check \"(= ((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_fx_success_errno\\\" [:int :int :int] :int {:capture-native-error true}) 1 2 3) [6 7777])\" \"true\")\n(public-check \"(try ((jolt.ffi/__cfn \\\"joltffi_absent\\\" [] :int)) (catch Throwable e (boolean (re-find #\\\"no entry\\\" (ex-message e)))))\" \"true\")\n(public-check \"(jolt.ffi/string->ptr nil)\" \"0\")\n(public-check \"(let [p (jolt.ffi/string->ptr \\\"abc\\\")] (try (jolt.ffi/ptr->string p 4) (finally (jolt.ffi/free p))))\" \"\\\"abc\\\"\")\n(public-check \"(let [p (jolt.ffi/alloc 8)] (jolt.ffi/free p) (jolt.ffi/__size p))\" \"0\")\n(printf \"gambitffi-public: ~a check(s), ~a failure(s)\\n\" checks failures)\n(if (= failures 0) (begin (display \"gambitffi-public: PASS — :gambit compiler + native gsi\\n\") (exit 0)) (exit 1))\n  (let loop ((hs joltffi-native-handles))\n    (cond ((null? hs) #f)\n          ((string=? (caar hs) path) (cdar hs))\n          (else (loop (cdr hs))))))\n\n;; process-global resolution (RTLD_DEFAULT). RTLD_LOCAL natives are\n;; deliberately invisible here — the one-way scoped-shadows-global guarantee.\n(define (joltffi-resolve-global name who)\n  (joltffi-dlerror)\n  (let ((a (joltffi-dlsym-global name)))\n    (if (joltffi-dlerror)\n        (error who\n               (string-append \"jolt.ffi: no entry for \\\"\" name\n                              \"\\\" — not in any loaded native and not in the process's global symbols\"))\n        a)))\n\n;; (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native sym) -> address | #f\n;; The compiler's emitted scoped probe (backend ffi-named-procedure-expr's\n;; scoped branch): the loaded handles in declaration order; #f sends the\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib.sha256\n\n# the present-but-unloadable candidate: a one-symbol dylib linked against a\n# dependency dylib this recipe then REMOVES, so dlopen fails with the loader's\n# own preserved reason (a missing dependency, not a missing file)\n$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture2.c\n\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-dep.c\n\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\n\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-unloadable.c $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib\n\trm $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\n\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib.sha256\n\n# bridge + fixtures, always current: the entry every gambitffi gate depends on\n.PHONY: gambitffi-force gambitffi-verify-digests\ngambitffi-force:\n\n#!/bin/sh\n# unbound-check.sh — every Scheme global the Gambit boot references is defined\n# (POSIX sh). The driver for host/gambit/unbound-check.ss; `make gambitunbound`.\n#\n# Regenerates the full-profile boot, compiles it to the js target (the shipped\n# web REPL's target, and the one whose base library is what the linker checks\n# against), then links with -warnings, which is where Gambit reports every\n# global referenced by the unit and defined nowhere. The link log goes to the\n# Chez script, which subtracts what the boot defines at runtime and compares\n# the rest with the allowlist. Flags pass through:\n#   --regen   rewrite host/gambit/unbound-allowlist.txt from the report\n#   --list    print every unbound name and its classification\n#\n# Compile only, no C compiler and no node: `gsc -c` writes JavaScript text and\n# `-link` the link file. About 75s on the full boot — the seed is what takes\n# the time.\n#\n# Resolution mirrors the other gambit gates: JOLT_GSC (the Makefile hands down\n# $(GAMBIT_GSC)), else brew's gambit-scheme. NEVER bare gsc, which is\n# Ghostscript on a brew machine. JOLT_CHEZ as in mirror-drift-check.sh.\nroot=\"$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")/../..\" && pwd)\"\ncd \"$root\" || exit 1\n\nif [ -z \"${JOLT_GSC:-}\" ]; then\n  prefix=\"$(brew --prefix gambit-scheme 2>/dev/null)\"\n  JOLT_GSC=\"$prefix/bin/gsc\"\nfi\nif [ ! -x \"$JOLT_GSC\" ]; then\n  echo \"gambit unbound: no gsc found (JOLT_GSC or brew gambit-scheme)\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nif [ -z \"${JOLT_CHEZ:-}\" ]; then\n  for c in chez chezscheme; do\n    if command -v \"$c\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n      JOLT_CHEZ=\"$c\"\n      break\n    fi\n  done\n  if [ -z \"${JOLT_CHEZ:-}\" ]; then\n    echo \"gambit unbound: no Chez Scheme executable found on PATH\" >&2\n    exit 1\n  fi\nfi\n\ntmp=\"$(mktemp -d)\" || exit 1\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$tmp\"' EXIT INT TERM\n\n\"$JOLT_CHEZ\" --script host/gambit/gen-boot.ss full > \"$tmp/gen-boot.log\" 2>&1 || {\n  cat \"$tmp/gen-boot.log\" >&2\n  echo \"gambit unbound: gen-boot.ss failed\" >&2\n  exit 1\n}\n\n# From host/gambit: boot-full.ss ##includes its files relative to itself, and\n# irregex.scm's own includes resolve from there too.\nif ! (cd host/gambit && \"$JOLT_GSC\" -target js -c -o \"$tmp/boot.js\" boot-full.ss) \\\n     > \"$tmp/compile.log\" 2>&1; then\n  tail -40 \"$tmp/compile.log\" >&2\n  echo \"gambit unbound: the boot does not compile — see above\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nif ! \"$JOLT_GSC\" -target js -warnings -link -o \"$tmp/boot_.js\" \"$tmp/boot.js\" \\\n     > \"$tmp/link.log\" 2>&1; then\n  tail -40 \"$tmp/link.log\" >&2\n  echo \"gambit unbound: the link step failed — see above\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n\"$JOLT_CHEZ\" --script host/gambit/unbound-check.ss \"$tmp/link.log\" \"$@\"\n;; unbound-check.ss — every Scheme global the Gambit boot references is defined.\n;;\n;; The boot ##include-splices most of host/chez, and a Chez-side name that\n;; reaches a shared file is an UNBOUND GLOBAL on Gambit: nothing fails at load,\n;; the first call raises \"Unbound variable: x\" with no jolt context, and — the\n;; part this gate exists for — nothing in the Chez suite can see it. mirrordrift\n;; compares procedures defined in BOTH rt.ss and rt-core.ss, so a NEW name (a\n;; parameter host-contract.ss started reading, an R6RS list op a shared file\n;; picked up) is invisible to it. `make gambiteval` had every row failing for\n;; two weeks that way (jolt-cw2p).\n;;\n;; The oracle is Gambit's own linker: `gsc -warnings -link` reports every global\n;; referenced by the compiled unit and defined nowhere, after full macro\n;; expansion — exact, with no free-variable analysis of our own to get wrong.\n;; unbound-check.sh runs the compile and link and hands this script the link\n;; log. Two things the linker cannot know are folded in here:\n;;\n;;   - a record's constructor/predicate/accessors come from the shim's\n;;     define-record-type translator (prelude-shims.ss), which EVALS them into\n;;     the interaction environment at boot, so the compiler never sees a\n;;     define for them. Derived here from every define-record-type form in the\n;;     booted manifest, by the translator's own naming rule.\n;;   - an uninterned #:gN name is never a missing definition. It is the mark of\n;;     Gambit's case-lambda expander dropping the rest parameter of a two-clause\n;;     (fixed n / variadic n) fn (backend_scheme.clj emit-fn has the story), and\n;;     it always fails: the fix is the emitter's merge, never an allowlist line.\n;;\n;; What is left is compared against host/gambit/unbound-allowlist.txt: names\n;; referenced from paths this target never takes (the excluded java/ tree's\n;; helpers behind capability checks, gsi runtime internals the js link file\n;; does not carry). Like the portability allowlist, the list only shrinks\n;; truthfully — a line whose name is now defined is STALE and fails the gate.\n;;\n;; Modes:\n;;   <link-log>            gate — exit 1 on an unallowlisted name, a stale line,\n;;                         or a #:gN name\n;;   <link-log> --regen    rewrite the allowlist: comments and still-valid lines\n;;                         kept in place, stale lines dropped, new names appended\n;;   <link-log> --list     print every unbound name and how it was classified\n(import (chezscheme))\n(include \"host/chez/gate-scan-lib.ss\")\n\n(define allowlist-path \"host/gambit/unbound-allowlist.txt\")\n(define boot-path \"host/gambit/boot-full.ss\")\n\n;; ---- the linker's report ----------------------------------------------------\n;; Two lines per warning:\n;;   *** WARNING -- \"NAME\" is not defined,\n;;   ***            referenced in: (\"FILE\" ...)\n;; A reference from the Gambit runtime library itself (_gambit.js names a few of\n;; its own internals the js link file does not carry) is Gambit's business, not\n;; the boot's: only a reference from the compiled boot counts.\n(define (quoted-strings line)\n  (let ((n (string-length line)))\n    (let loop ((i 0) (acc '()))\n      (cond ((>= i n) (reverse acc))\n            ((char=? (string-ref line i) #\\\")\n             (let scan ((j (+ i 1)))\n               (cond ((>= j n) (reverse acc))\n                     ((char=? (string-ref line j) #\\\")\n                      (loop (+ j 1) (cons (substring line (+ i 1) j) acc)))\n                     (else (scan (+ j 1))))))\n            (else (loop (+ i 1) acc))))))\n\n(define (runtime-library? path)\n  (gs-string-suffix? \"/_gambit.js\" path))\n\n(define (parse-link-log path)\n  (let ((lines (call-with-input-file path\n                 (lambda (p)\n                   (let loop ((acc '()))\n                     (let ((l (get-line p)))\n                       (if (eof-object? l) (reverse acc) (loop (cons l acc)))))))))\n    (let loop ((ls lines) (acc '()))\n      (cond\n        ((null? ls) (reverse acc))\n        ((and (gs-string-prefix? \"*** WARNING -- \" (car ls))\n              (gs-string-contains? (car ls) \"is not defined\")\n              (pair? (cdr ls))\n              (gs-string-contains? (cadr ls) \"referenced in:\"))\n         (let ((name (car (quoted-strings (car ls))))\n               (files (quoted-strings (cadr ls))))\n           (loop (cddr ls)\n                 (if (exists (lambda (f) (not (runtime-library? f))) files)\n                     (cons name acc)\n                     acc))))\n        (else (loop (cdr ls) acc))))))\n\n;; ---- the booted manifest ------------------------------------------------------\n;; boot-full.ss (generated by gen-boot.ss) ##includes every file of the boot,\n;; some of which ##include further (repl-main's boot-active, records-gambit's\n;; none). Followed here relative to the including file, like Gambit does.\n(define (includes-of path)\n  (let loop ((fs (gs-read-forms path)) (acc '()))\n    (if (null? fs)\n        (reverse acc)\n        (let ((d (car fs)))\n          (loop (cdr fs)\n                (if (and (pair? d) (eq? (car d) 'gambit-ns:include)\n                         (pair? (cdr d)) (string? (cadr d)))\n                    (cons (cadr d) acc)\n                    acc))))))\n\n(define (resolve-include from rel)\n  (let ((dir (path-parent from)))\n    (if (string=? dir \"\") rel (string-append dir \"/\" rel))))\n\n(define (manifest root)\n  (let walk ((p root))\n    (cons p (apply append (map (lambda (r) (walk (resolve-include p r))) (includes-of p))))))\n\n;; ---- names the record translator evals at boot --------------------------------\n;; make-jolt-record-type (prelude-shims.ss): make-<name> / <name>? unless the\n;; spec names them, <name>-<field> unless the field spec names its accessor, and\n;; a -set! mutator (named or derived) for a MUTABLE field only. The translator's\n;; own define-syntax is skipped: a template is not a definition.\n(define (record-names d)\n  (let* ((spec (cadr d))\n         (name (if (pair? spec) (car spec) spec))\n         (nstr (symbol->string name))\n         (ctor (if (pair? spec) (cadr spec) (string->symbol (string-append \"make-\" nstr))))\n         (pred (if (pair? spec) (caddr spec) (string->symbol (string-append nstr \"?\"))))\n         (fields (let ((c (assq 'fields (cddr d)))) (if c (cdr c) '()))))\n    (cons ctor\n          (cons pred\n                (apply append\n                       (map (lambda (fs)\n                              (let* ((kind (if (pair? fs) (car fs) 'immutable))\n                                     (f (if (pair? fs) (cadr fs) fs))\n                                     (acc (if (and (pair? fs) (pair? (cddr fs)))\n                                              (caddr fs)\n                                              (string->symbol (string-append nstr \"-\" (symbol->string f)))))\n                                     (setter (if (and (pair? fs) (pair? (cddr fs)) (pair? (cdddr fs)))\n                                                 (cadddr fs)\n                                                 (string->symbol (string-append (symbol->string acc) \"-set!\")))))\n                                (if (eq? kind 'mutable) (list acc setter) (list acc))))\n                            fields))))))\n\n(define (record-generated-names files)\n  (let ((h (make-hashtable string-hash string=?)))\n    (define (walk d)\n      (when (pair? d)\n        (cond\n          ((eq? (car d) 'define-syntax) #f)\n          ((and (eq? (car d) 'define-record-type) (pair? (cdr d)))\n           (for-each (lambda (s) (hashtable-set! h (symbol->string s) #t)) (record-names d)))\n          (else (let loop ((x d))\n                  (when (pair? x) (walk (car x)) (loop (cdr x))))))))\n    (for-each (lambda (f) (for-each walk (gs-read-forms f))) files)\n    h))\n;; ffi.ss — the runtime side of jolt's foreign-function interface (jolt.ffi).\n;;\n;; A jolt LIBRARY binds native code itself: it loads a shared object and declares\n;; typed foreign functions, then exposes a Clojure API. The TYPED CALL is lowered\n;; at compile time to a Chez `foreign-procedure` by the backend (the\n;; `jolt.ffi/foreign-fn` special form) — this file provides everything that does\n;; NOT need compile-time types: loading libraries, allocating/reading/writing\n;; foreign memory, and string/pointer marshaling. All exposed under `jolt.ffi`.\n;;\n;; A foreign pointer is a Chez machine address (an exact integer / uptr), the same\n;; representation `void*` arguments and results use, so pointers flow between\n;; foreign-fn calls and these helpers transparently.\n\n;; --- a jolt value used AS a string -------------------------------------------\n;; jolt-str-render-one is the `str` coercion, and it renders nil as \"\". That is\n;; right for str and it is right where the boundary copies a VALUE — string->ptr\n;; and with-c-string document exactly that. It is wrong wherever the string names\n;; something, because an absent name silently became an empty one: dlopen(\"\"), a\n;; foreign type called \"\", a zero-byte write that reports 0 octets written and is\n;; indistinguishable from writing \"\".\n;;\n;; nil has no representation in any of those positions. Where it DOES have one it\n;; is already used — NULL, in a :string argument and in string->ptr — so the split\n;; is between \"absence means NULL here\" and \"absence means nothing here\", and this\n;; is the second. Every other value keeps the coercion, so 42 still names \"42\".\n(define (ffi-str-arg what x)\n  (if (jolt-nil? x)\n      (throw-jvm 'IllegalArgumentException\n                 (string-append \"jolt.ffi: \" what \" must be a string, got nil\"))\n      (jolt-str-render-one x)))\n\n;; --- loading shared objects --------------------------------------------------\n;; (jolt.ffi/load-library name) loads a .so/.dylib by name (resolved by the OS\n;; loader against the standard search paths). A library typically calls this once\n;; at load with a platform-specific name. (load-library) with no name (or #f)\n;; makes the running process's own symbols (libc, sockets) resolvable.\n;;\n;; NEITHER form may call (sa-load-shared-object #f) any more: Chez resolves\n;; foreign-entry most-recently-loaded first, and re-loading the process-global\n;; handle RE-PROMOTES it above every :jolt/native loaded so far — which is how\n;; Apple's /usr/lib/libboringssl.dylib (a global-namespace resident that exports\n;; the whole EVP_* set) came to serve jolt-lang/crypto's OpenSSL bindings and\n;; abort in digest_update. The boot already loaded the global handle once\n;; (jolt-foreign-proc-safe, rt.ss); process symbols resolve through that without\n;; any reload. A NAMED library goes through the scoped loader below — RTLD_LOCAL\n;; + a registered handle — so its symbols are reachable by its own defcfns and\n;; invisible to everyone else's.\n(define (ffi-load-library . args)\n  (cond\n    ((or (null? args) (jolt-nil? (car args)))\n     jolt-nil)                                   ; boot's global handle suffices\n    ;; The documented per-OS map spec — {:darwin \"…\" :linux \"…\" :windows \"…\"} —\n    ;; select this platform's entry. (It was documented but never implemented:\n    ;; the map rendered to a string and dlopen'd garbage; surfaced auditing the\n    ;; scoped-resolution change.) A map with no entry for this platform raises,\n    ;; naming the platform, rather than silently loading nothing. :mac is\n    ;; babashka.ffi's spelling of :darwin and selects the same entry.\n    ((jolt-map? (car args))\n     (let* ((spec (car args))\n            (family (sa-os-family))\n            (key (case family ((macos) \"darwin\") ((windows) \"windows\") (else \"linux\")))\n            (name (jolt-get-dispatch spec (keyword #f key) jolt-nil))\n            (name (if (and (jolt-nil? name) (eq? family 'macos))\n                      (jolt-get-dispatch spec (keyword #f \"mac\") jolt-nil)\n                      name)))\n       (when (jolt-nil? name)\n         (jolt-throw (jolt-ex-info\n                       (string-append \"jolt.ffi/load-library: no :\" key\n                                      \" entry in the per-OS spec\")\n                       spec)))\n       (ffi-library-map (ffi-load-candidates (ffi-candidate-list name)))))\n    (else (ffi-library-map (ffi-load-candidates (ffi-candidate-list (car args)))))))\n\n;; A candidate spec is one name or an ORDERED list of them. babashka.ffi takes a\n;; vector of candidates in every position a name goes (including inside the\n;; per-OS map), because the same library is spelled differently across distros —\n;; libcrypto.so.3 here, libcrypto.so.1.1 there. A single name stays a single\n;; name; anything seqable becomes the list to try in order.\n(define (ffi-candidate-list name)\n  (if (or (pvec? name) (jolt-seq? name) (jolt-lazyseq? name))\n      (map (lambda (c) (ffi-str-arg \"library candidate\" c)) (seq->list (jolt-seq name)))\n      (list (jolt-str-render-one name))))\n\n;; Try each candidate in order; answer the one that loaded.\n;;\n;; A load that finds NOTHING must raise: callers probe candidate lists with\n;; try/catch around load-library (jolt.mvn-http), and the pre-scoped-loader\n;; implementation raised through sa-load-shared-object. Silently returning nil\n;; turned every fallback list into \"first candidate wins, loaded or not\". The\n;; error names every candidate tried, since \"cannot load libcrypto.so.3\" alone\n;; hides the three other spellings that were also attempted.\n(define (ffi-load-candidates cands)\n  (let loop ((cs cands))\n    (cond\n      ((null? cs)\n26:(define (ffi-str-arg what x)\n81:      (map (lambda (c) (ffi-str-arg \"library candidate\" c)) (seq->list (jolt-seq name)))\n358:    (ffi-system-library-candidates (ffi-str-arg \"load-system-library name\" name)))))\n364:(define (ffi-loaded? name)\n365:  (if (jolt-ffi-load-native (ffi-str-arg \"loaded? name\" name)) #t #f))\n672:(define (jolt-ffi-defining-libraries sym)\n675:    (map car (jolt-ffi-native-definers (ffi-str-arg \"symbol\" sym))))))\n685:(define (ffi-type->chez kw)\n686:  (let ((n (if (keyword-t? kw) (keyword-t-name kw) (ffi-str-arg \"foreign type\" kw))))\n820:  (let ((ct (ffi-type->chez ty)))\n832:  (let ((ct (ffi-type->chez ty)))\n841:(define (ffi-sizeof ty) (sa-foreign-sizeof (ffi-chez-width (ffi-type->chez ty))))\n870:  (let* ((bv (string->utf8 (ffi-str-arg \"write-bytes value\" s))) (n (bytevector-length bv)) (p (jnum->exact ptr)))\n1055:  (let* ((ct (ffi-type->chez type))\n1104:       (let* ((ct (ffi-type->chez type)) (v (jolt-array-vec arr))\n1616:(define ffi-find-symbol\n1619:     (let* ((n (ffi-str-arg \"symbol\" sym))\n1627:         (ffi-find-symbol sym)\n1628:         (let* ((n (ffi-str-arg \"symbol\" sym))\n1739:(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"loaded?\" (lambda (n) (if (ffi-loaded? n) #t #f)))\n1741:(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"defining-libraries\" jolt-ffi-defining-libraries)\n1760:                           (ffi-str-arg \"system-library-candidates name\" n)))))\n1766:         (map (lambda (c) (ffi-str-arg \"load-failure-note candidate\" c))\n1769:(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"find-symbol\" ffi-find-symbol)\n| `gambitffi-errno-check` | (via `make gambitffi`) | **PASS** (`9 check(s), 0 failure(s)`) |\n| `gambitffi-load-failure-smoke` | (via `make gambitffi`) | **PASS** (`14 check(s), 0 failure(s)`) |\n| `gambitffi` (aggregate) | (via `make gambitffi`) | **PASS** (`all stage-1 qualified-tier gates green`) |\n| `gambitcheck` | (via `make gambitcheck`) | **PASS** (`0 failure(s) — gambit adapter + shims verified on native gsi`) |\n| `gambitkernel` | (via `make gambitkernel`) | **PASS** (`0 failure(s) — booted kernel + natives verified on native gsi`) |\n| `gambiteval` | (via `make gambiteval`) | **PASS** (`0 failure(s) — jolt compiles and evaluates on native gsi`) |\n| `gambitseedcheck` | `sh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 180 make gambitseedcheck ...` | **PASS** (`gambit seed is current with the sources`) |\n| `gambitgencheck` | (via `make gambitgencheck`) | **PASS** (`records-gambit.ss is current with the records files`) |\n| `gambittwins` | (via `make gambittwins`) | **PASS** (`13 call-position macro(s), every one twinned in eval-fns.ss`) |\n| `adaptercheck` | (via `make adaptercheck`) | **PASS** (`149 contract names checked against the combined env`) |\n| `gambitvars` | `gsi host/gambit/unbound-vars.ss < /dev/null` | **PASS** (`3625 var cell(s) after boot, 4 unbound (4 allowlisted)`) |\n| `gambitstatics` | `sh host/gambit/seed-statics.sh` | **PASS** (`19 static(s) and 30 constructor(s); 11 unresolved (11 allowlisted)`) |\n| Chez `ffi-binding-test.ss` | `scheme --script test/chez/ffi-binding-test.ss` | **PASS** (`74/74 passed`) |\n| Chez `ffi-widths-test.sh` | `sh test/chez/ffi-widths-test.sh .../scheme` | **PASS** (`86/86 passed`) |\n| Chez `ffi-native-error-test.sh` (current seeds) | `sh test/chez/ffi-native-error-test.sh .../scheme` | **39/41** (same 2 loopback-socket rows blocked by sandbox `bind`) |\n| Chez `ffi-native-error-test.ss` (untouched `a6852ef8` base seeds) | `python3 p1b-stage1/evidence/prepare-base-seed-comparison.py` + `scheme --script /tmp/p1b-base-errno/errno.ss` | **39/41** (reproduces exact same 2 loopback-socket failures on base seeds) |\n| Negative controls | `python3 p1b-stage1/evidence/negative-checks.py` and `gsi p1b-stage1/evidence/no-bridge.ss` in `/tmp` | **PASS** (corrupted digest rejected before compile; watchdog returns `124`; missing bridge fails closed with documented message) |\n\nRECOMMENDATION: ACCEPT-WITH-FIXES (1. Fix P2 F1 in `host/gambit/host-ffi.ss:214` by replacing unbound `bytevector->u8-list` with `u8vector->list` in `joltffi-read-bytes` and adding a non-UTF-8 `read-bytes` check to `host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-public.ss`; 2. Optionally address P3 F2–F4: `nil`-guard string-naming args in `host/gambit/host-ffi.ss`, add `\"host-ffi.ss\"` to `host/gambit/profiles.ss` + bridge symbols to `host/gambit/unbound-allowlist.txt`, and fix the `libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib` prerequisite list in `Makefile:2126-2127`).\n\n;; gen-boot.ss — write host/gambit/boot-<profile>.ss for a build profile.\n;;\n;; Run on CHEZ from the repo root (make gambitweb PROFILE=... does this):\n;;   chez --script host/gambit/gen-boot.ss repl\n;;\n;; Gambit resolves ##include at expansion time, so which files a build carries\n;; cannot be a runtime choice — the boot has to be generated. Same reasoning as\n;; the seed and records-gambit.ss: derive it on Chez, check nothing by hand.\n;;\n;; boot.ss owns the load order; profiles.ss says which of its files are optional\n;; and which profile keeps which groups. Excluded files are dropped from the\n;; include list, and every clojure.core name they define is bound to a raise\n;; naming the group — read out of the files themselves, so the error surface\n;; cannot drift from the code.\n\n(import (chezscheme))\n(print-brackets #f)\n\n(define args (command-line-arguments))\n(define profile-name\n  (if (null? args)\n      (begin (display \"usage: gen-boot.ss <profile>\\n\") (exit 1))\n      (string->symbol (car args))))\n\n(define (read-all f)\n  (with-input-from-file f\n    (lambda ()\n      (let loop ((acc '()))\n        (let ((x (read)))\n          (if (eof-object? x) (reverse acc) (loop (cons x acc))))))))\n\n;; ---- profiles.ss -----------------------------------------------------------\n\n(define spec (read-all \"host/gambit/profiles.ss\"))\n\n(define (section name)\n  (let loop ((fs spec))\n    (cond ((null? fs) (error 'gen-boot \"section missing from profiles.ss\" name))\n          ((and (pair? (car fs)) (eq? (caar fs) name)) (cdar fs))\n          (else (loop (cdr fs))))))\n\n(define group-specs (section 'groups))     ; (name label (file ...))\n(define profile-specs (section 'profiles)) ; (name (group ...))\n\n(define (profile-names) (map car profile-specs))\n\n(define kept-groups\n  (let loop ((ps profile-specs))\n    (cond ((null? ps)\n           (display \"gen-boot: unknown profile \")\n           (display profile-name)\n           (display \"; profiles.ss lists \")\n           (write (profile-names))\n           (newline)\n           (exit 1))\n          ((eq? (caar ps) profile-name) (cadar ps))\n          (else (loop (cdr ps))))))\n\n(define excluded-groups\n  (let loop ((gs group-specs) (acc '()))\n    (cond ((null? gs) (reverse acc))\n          ((memq (caar gs) kept-groups) (loop (cdr gs) acc))\n          (else (loop (cdr gs) (cons (car gs) acc))))))\n\n(define excluded-files\n  (apply append (map caddr excluded-groups)))\n\n;; ---- the names an excluded group takes with it ------------------------------\n;; Scan for (def-var! \"clojure.core\" \"name\" — the one way a host file publishes\n;; a core name, and how the emitted prelude publishes every one of them.\n\n(define core-def-prefix\n  (string-append \"(def-var! \" (string #\\\") \"clojure.core\" (string #\\\")\n                 \" \" (string #\\\")))\n\n(define (name-end text start)\n  (let scan ((j start))\n    (cond ((>= j (string-length text)) j)\n          ((char=? (string-ref text j) (string-ref (string #\\\") 0)) j)\n          (else (scan (+ j 1))))))\n\n(define (file-core-names path)\n  (let ((full (string-append \"host/gambit/\" path)))\n    (if (not (file-exists? full))\n        (list)\n        (let ((text (call-with-input-file full (lambda (p) (get-string-all p)))))\n          (let loop ((i 0) (acc (list)))\n            (let ((hit (find-substring core-def-prefix text i)))\n              (if (not hit)\n                  (reverse acc)\n                  (let* ((start (+ hit (string-length core-def-prefix)))\n                         (end (name-end text start)))\n                    (loop end (cons (substring text start end) acc))))))))))\n\n(define (find-substring needle hay from)\n  (let ((nl (string-length needle)) (hl (string-length hay)))\n    (let loop ((i from))\n      (cond ((> (+ i nl) hl) #f)\n            ((string=? (substring hay i (+ i nl)) needle) i)\n            (else (loop (+ i 1)))))))\n\n;; A name the KEPT files also define is not missing — the kernel or another\n;; group still provides it.\n(define kept-names\n  (let loop ((gs group-specs) (acc '()))\n    (cond ((null? gs) acc)\n          ((memq (caar gs) kept-groups)\n           (loop (cdr gs) (append (apply append (map file-core-names (caddar gs))) acc)))\n          (else (loop (cdr gs) acc)))))\n\n(define (missing-names-of group)\n  (let ((names (apply append (map file-core-names (caddr group)))))\n    ;; dedupe, and drop anything still provided elsewhere\n    (let loop ((ns names) (seen '()) (acc '()))\n      (cond ((null? ns) (reverse acc))\n            ((member (car ns) seen) (loop (cdr ns) seen acc))\n            ((member (car ns) kept-names) (loop (cdr ns) (cons (car ns) seen) acc))\n            (else (loop (cdr ns) (cons (car ns) seen) (cons (car ns) acc)))))))\n\n;; ---- write the boot --------------------------------------------------------\n\n(define boot-lines\n  (let ((p (open-input-file \"host/gambit/boot.ss\")))\n    (let loop ((acc '()))\n      (let ((l (get-line p)))\n        (if (eof-object? l)\n            (begin (close-port p) (reverse acc))\n            (loop (cons l acc)))))))\n\n(define (include-line? l)\n  (find-substring \"(##include \\\"\" l 0))\n\n(define (included-path l)\n  (let* ((s (find-substring \"\\\"\" l 0))\n         (start (+ s 1))\n         (end (let scan ((j start))\n                (if (char=? (string-ref l j) #\\\") j (scan (+ j 1))))))\n    (substring l start end)))\n\n(define boot-include-paths\n  (let loop ((ls boot-lines) (acc (list)))\n    (cond ((null? ls) (reverse acc))\n          ((find-substring \"(##include \\\"\" (car ls) 0)\n           (loop (cdr ls) (cons (included-path (car ls)) acc)))\n          (else (loop (cdr ls) acc)))))\n\n;; ---- the SCHEME-level names an excluded file takes with it -------------------\n;; A booted file may call an excluded file's procedure directly, which no core\n;; var covers: the reader builds a #\"...\" literal through jolt-re-pattern, and\n;; the class model probes jolt-regex?. Same rule as the hand-written degradations\n;; in host-vars.ss — a PREDICATE answers #f, because a value cannot be of a type\n;; this build does not carry, and anything else raises.\n;;\n;; seed/ files are skipped: their defines are per-var mangled names reached only\n;; through var cells, never called by name from a booted file.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
