is how chunk-first took `defn` down for two weeks while\n;; every gate stayed green.\n;;\n;; Compared against host/gambit/unbound-vars-allowlist.txt, which names the vars\n;; this target cannot bind and no path reaches (the compiler image's build and\n;; image entry points, the host IO seams behind reader protocols). The list\n;; only shrinks truthfully: a line whose var is bound now is STALE and fails.\n;; Chez has exactly two unbound cells after the same load — the unquote markers\n Makefile                              |  2 +-\n host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-public.ss   | 16 ++++++++++++++\n host/gambit/host-ffi.ss               | 34 +++++++++++++++++++-----------\n host/gambit/profiles.ss               |  3 ++-\n host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss |  2 +-\n host/gambit/unbound-allowlist.txt     | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 6 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)\nhost/gambit/ffi/joltffi-fixture2.c: OK\nhost/gambit/ffi/joltffi-dep.c: OK\nhost/gambit/ffi/joltffi-unloadable.c: OK\nhost/gambit/ffi/TOOLCHAIN.sha256: OK\ncp host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm host/gambit/ffi/generated-shims.scm build/gambit-ffi/\ncd build/gambit-ffi && sh ../../host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 120 /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8/bin/gsc -dynamic -keep-temp joltffi-bridge.scm\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
